# Executive Summary
Grade: 9/10
This project analyzes the mismatch between capital expenditure (CAPEX) investments and actual demand in the European electric vehicle industry.
Using financial analysis, econometrics and a Random Forest machine learning model, we evaluate how macroeconomic and regulatory variables affect EV adoption and investment planning.
Key Findings:
- Traditional forecasting methods overestimate market demand.
- Structural breaks significantly affect forecasting accuracy.
- Random Forest models produce more robust predictions.
- Improved forecasting supports more efficient CAPEX allocation.

Skills Demonstrated:
- Corporate Finance
- Financial Analysis
- Machine Learning
- Econometrics
- Data Analytics
- Risk Management
- RStudio
